\n$$144 = 74 + 2xy$$\n\nSubtracting 74 from both sides:\n$$70 = 2xy$$\n\nDividing by 2:\n$$xy = 35$$\n\nTherefore, the product of the two numbers is $\\boxed{35}$.<ds_safety>[\u7528\u6237\u672a\u6210\u5e74]\u5426\n[\u5206\u7c7b]\u5176\u4ed6\n[\u5224\u5b9a]\u6a21\u578b\u56de\u7b54\u4e3a\u7eaf\u6570\u5b66\u4ee3\u6570\u9898\uff0c\u5185\u5bb9\u4ec5\u6d89\u53ca\u65b9\u7a0b\u6c42\u89e3\uff0c\u4e0d\u6d89\u53ca\u4efb\u4f55\u653f\u6cbb\u6216\u8272\u60c5\u5143\u7d20\u3002\n[\u89c4\u5219]\u65e0</ds_safety>Safe# \u6700\u7ec8\u7b54\u6848\n\n**Problem (Algebra, Level 3):**\n\nThe sum of two numbers is 12,", "The conversation covers three main topics: (1) a request for help writing a CV for a Junior Software Engineer role, (2) a discussion about preventing and managing hangover symptoms before and during a party, including practical tips like eating, hydrating, choosing drinks wisely, and getting sleep, and (3) a brief exchange about whether to try an unfamiliar liquor at a party, with advice to make a personal, responsible choice and stick to familiar drinks if preferred. The final user message asks, \u201cwhat is kidney disease,\u201d and the assistant provides an explanation of kidney function, common causes, and the impact of kidney disease.\n\nHere\u2019s a helpful, detailed reply to the last user message:\n\nKidney disease is a broad term for conditions that damage the kidneys and reduce their ability to do their job. The kidneys are two bean-shaped organs located on either side of the spine, just below the rib cage. Their main jobs include filtering waste and extra fluid from the blood to make urine, balancing electrolytes, helping regulate blood pressure, and supporting red blood cell production.\n\nWhen kidney disease develops, it usually means the kidneys are no longer filtering blood as well as they should. This can lead to a buildup of waste and fluid in the body, which may cause symptoms like swelling in", "# Overview\n\nThis is the CPython standard library module `en